WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.110
- Everything that happened yesterday,

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.713
that means nothing.

00:00:06.477 --> 00:00:08.727
(applause)

00:00:10.778 --> 00:00:13.195
(slow music)

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.453
When you're 19,

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.680
and you can spend seven full
years learning your craft,

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.600
meeting people that are
mentors, being patient,

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.840
and you wake up and you're 26 years old,

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.712
you have your entire life in front of you

00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:34.770
and you've done great foundational work

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.940
to go on and then be successful.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:37.840
I just don't get it,

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.986
I don't get why people
think at 18, 22, 30,

00:00:41.986 --> 00:00:43.320
that they have to have
their life figured out

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.630
when they live to 90 and 100.

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:46.520
- If you could give any
quick piece of advice.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:47.353
- [Gary] It's patience.

00:00:47.353 --> 00:00:48.186
- I'm like lost in life.

00:00:48.186 --> 00:00:49.349
- [Gary] It's patience.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.657
You can't be lost in life
when you're this young.

00:00:51.657 --> 00:00:54.000
Should you actually have
everything figured out

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.140
18 or 20 percent into your life?

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.010
Absolutely not,

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:58.530
more importantly than that,

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.040
your life evolves and
changes as you get older.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.000
Too many kids don't
take advantage of time.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.820
They're in such a rush to find it,

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:08.831
or be doing it,

00:01:08.831 --> 00:01:11.440
that they don't take advantage
of the thing they have.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.250
Figuring everything out is a forever game.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.430
Have you figured out how awesome

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:16.780
you're gonna be as a grandma

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.270
when you're still not a grandma?

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:21.700
Whether it's your parents
or yourself, or people,

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:23.920
everybody's trying to
prove something so early.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.661
It's the pressures of society,

00:01:25.661 --> 00:01:28.640
the pressures of your siblings,

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.220
and most of all the
pressures of your parents.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:33.010
So many of you are scared to fail,

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:35.630
because your dads gonna
make you feel bad about it.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:37.890
And I have empathy for that, that sucks.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.160
I'm very fascinated by negative energy

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.180
that is not cut-outable.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.750
You need to put your fuckin' earpods in

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.390
and listen to positive 24/7
and it'll get you through that.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:48.744
Or this ideological thing that the media

00:01:48.744 --> 00:01:50.610
or culture has put in your head

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.910
of what you're supposed to be,

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:53.020
or how you're supposed to roll,

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.130
or what's supposed to be happening

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:55.900
at this point is ludicrous.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:56.940
You're not lost in life,

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.259
you're just early in the process.

00:01:58.259 --> 00:02:01.290
(upbeat music)

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:02.740
You just don't meet 90 year olds

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:03.980
that talk about how pumped they are

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:05.910
that they made an extra
hundred thousand dollars.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:06.743
They don't exist.

00:02:06.743 --> 00:02:08.810
They talk about regret.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.010
I wish I did,

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:12.350
literally, inevitably, I do this.

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:14.500
I wish is the opening line.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.960
The judgment you put on yourself

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:19.654
that is actually being
fabricated by outside forces

00:02:19.654 --> 00:02:21.150
is to me the thing

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.710
that I'm trying to
fundamentally break down.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.720
Just fundamentally
trying to break it down.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.000
Everybody's judging
themselves way too early.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.369
You can literally do nothing
for the next eight years,

00:02:30.369 --> 00:02:32.090
and be a child.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:33.213
Time is your asset.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.320
The one thing a 20 year old has over me

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.900
is 20 fuckin' years.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:38.940
But you don't think that,

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:41.200
because when you're 22 you
don't think 31 is young.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.770
- Maybe there's a problem with youth.

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:43.870
- Yeah, I mean that's,

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.700
everybody's got strengths and weaknesses.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.120
What a 60 year old has is experience,

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:50.340
but doesn't have time.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.890
What youth has is time.

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.891
You can literally do four different things

00:02:53.891 --> 00:02:55.380
over the next two years,

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.350
six months at a time,

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:59.780
to figure out everything that
you think you might like,

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.624
you should try to do.

00:03:01.624 --> 00:03:03.920
But that's not what people tell you to do.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:05.563
- Yeah, they tell you to do your job.

00:03:05.563 --> 00:03:06.396
- 100 percent.

00:03:06.396 --> 00:03:08.810
What I would do is gather as
many experiences as possible.

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:10.722
Go and travel and learn.

00:03:10.722 --> 00:03:13.032
Go and start that business
that you've always wanted.

00:03:13.032 --> 00:03:15.270
Hook up with those three teammates

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.920
and start that band you've always wanted.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.440
This is the time to be massively risk,

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.380
massively risk oriented.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:22.530
Pick something and fuckin' do it.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:23.490
You're a fuckin' young kid,

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:24.760
you can do all 19 things.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.570
If you're under 32, 33,

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:28.800
and you're devastated

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.110
that you don't have your life figured out,

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.930
you're just looking at
the game completely wrong.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.810
Take a breath, take a fuckin' breath.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:37.240
And so that's what I'm
trying to tell people.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:38.563
It's what you don't do

00:03:38.563 --> 00:03:41.380
that screws with you later on.

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:43.580
The reason you're not winning
and doing what you want

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.840
is somebody's opinion,

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.100
somebody's opinion of you

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:54.003
matters more to you than
your opinion of yourself.

00:03:55.793 --> 00:03:57.508
It's very true.

00:03:57.508 --> 00:03:59.758
(applause)

